<hi2txt label="Cruis'n USA">
  <!--
    Cruis'n USA (crusnusa) - Midway, 1994 (midvunit.cpp / V-Unit hardware).
    The HOT TIMES best-times boards are persisted natively to CMOS, which MAME
    saves as nvram\crusnusa\nvram (32768 bytes). There is one board PER COURSE
    plus a final overall cross-country ("SF TO WASHINGTON DC") board: 15 boards
    in all. Proven by matching the stored values to the on-screen boards
    (e.g. course #1 TVG 02:03:20; overall #1 TVG 28:30:54, #10 BDP 35:07:63).

    Boards begin at offset 0x0fe0, stored back-to-back, each 10 records x 0x20
    (32) bytes => 320 bytes per board, 15 boards = 4800 bytes (ends at 0x22a0,
    where the 0xff fill begins). Each 32-byte record is two 16-byte blocks:
      [0..2]   best time: 24-bit little-endian tick count @ ~55 Hz (value is
               repeated across the block; only the first LE word is read).
               Course boards fit in 2 bytes; the overall board needs 3.
      [3..15]  redundant copies of the tick -> skipped
      [16..27] 3 initials, each a 32-bit BIG-endian word with the ASCII char in
               the LOW byte, i.e. 00 00 00 <char>  (e.g. 00 00 00 54 = 'T')
      [28..31] char-count word (0x00000003) -> skipped

    Displayed time = trunc(tick * 20 / 11) centiseconds, shown as MM:SS:CC
    (verified against every board). All 14 course boards hold identical factory
    defaults, so board->course title order follows the game's attract/course
    sequence (SF -> Washington DC); the 15th board is the overall run.

    Authored by Pipmick @ CoinOPS.
  //-->

  <structure file="nvram">
    <check>
      <size>32768</size>
    </check>

    <elt size="4064" type="raw" id="HEADER"/>

    <loop count="10">
      <elt size="3"  type="int"  id="TICK0" endianness="little_endian"/>
      <elt size="13" type="raw"  id="TPAD0"/>
      <elt size="3"  type="raw"  id="PA0"/>
      <elt size="1"  type="text" id="C1_0"/>
      <elt size="3"  type="raw"  id="PB0"/>
      <elt size="1"  type="text" id="C2_0"/>
      <elt size="3"  type="raw"  id="PC0"/>
      <elt size="1"  type="text" id="C3_0"/>
      <elt size="4"  type="raw"  id="NLEN0"/>
    </loop>

    <loop count="10">
